# Class: obo:SWO_1100032 (BLAST)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1100032 "BLAST, or Basic Local Alignment Search Tool in full, is an algorithm for comparing primary biological sequence information, such as the amino-acid  sequences of different proteins or the nucleotides  of DNA sequences.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:SWO_1100032 "The Basic Local Alignment Search Tool (BLAST) finds regions of local similarity between sequences. The program compares nucleotide or protein sequences to sequence databases and calculates the statistical significance of matches. BLAST can be used to infer functional and evolutionary relationships between sequences as well as help identify members of gene families.")
AnnotationAssertion(dc:contributor obo:SWO_1100032 "Allyson Lister: added 'achieves objective' axioms for pairwise and multiple sequence alignment classes.")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:SWO_1100032 "BLAST")
